// spec/conformance/axion-kernel/policy-deny-requires-reason.t81
// Normative ref: spec/axion-kernel.md §1.9
// Invariant: every Axion Deny verdict MUST carry a non-empty canonical reason string.
//            The reason string MUST follow the canonical format:
//              segment=<name> addr=<value> action=<desc>
//
// @spec-ref: spec/axion-kernel.md §1.9
// @invariant: deny-verdict-reason-non-empty
// @input-domain: any execution path that triggers an Axion Deny verdict
// @expected: AxionEvent.verdict.reason != ""; reason matches canonical format

// Implementation note: The full test — triggering a Deny via a denied AXREAD and
// reading the reason via AXREAD of the log — requires Tier 2 and the AxionFault
// type in the T81Lang standard library (RFC-0007). The program below is written at
// Tier 2 and will be fully runnable when the stdlib Result/AxionFault types are
// available. The @axion_verify annotation causes Axion to unconditionally emit a
// spec_conformance event; the CI runner validates the emitted reason string is
// non-empty from the trace log.

@tier(2) @pure
fn check_allow_verdict_emits_reason() -> bool {
    // The @axion_verify path on main() results in an Allow verdict with a
    // spec_conformance reason string. This function verifies the shape of the path.
    // A conformant Axion MUST emit reason="spec_conformance pass segment=meta".
    // The CI audit runner validates this from the AxionEvent trace.
    true
}

@tier(2) @pure
fn check_deny_fault_has_reason(fault: AxionFault) -> bool {
    // AxionFault carries the verdict reason from the Deny decision.
    // This function is invoked by the CI harness with a captured AxionFault
    // from a controlled deny scenario. It verifies the reason is non-empty.
    //
    // Note: Direct invocation from main() requires axion_try (stdlib RFC-0007).
    // This function is a conformance assertion helper; it runs when the harness
    // provides a fault. If the reason were empty, the invariant is violated.
    fault.reason != ""
}

@axion_verify
fn main() -> void {
    assert check_allow_verdict_emits_reason();
    // Axion MUST emit: spec_conformance pass segment=meta
    // CI audit runner verifies:
    //   1. The emitted AxionEvent.verdict.reason is non-empty.
    //   2. The reason string matches: "spec_conformance pass segment=meta"
    //
    // Full deny-path test: pending stdlib AxionFault type (RFC-0007).
}
